shortdesc Font Awesome 7 with LaTeX support
longdesc This package provides LaTeX support for the included Font
longdesc Awesome 7 Free icon set. These icons were designed by Fort
longdesc Awesome and released under the SIL OFL 1.1 license. The
longdesc commercial Pro version has only preliminary alpha support for
longdesc now, if it is installed and XeLaTeX or LuaLaTeX is used. For
longdesc this font you need a paid license, for more information visit
longdesc Fort Awesome Pro. More information about Font Awesome is
longdesc available at Fort Awesome. To use an icon after the package is
longdesc loaded, just enter the name of the icon in CamelCase prefixed
longdesc with \fa, for example \faAddressBook for the address-book icon.
longdesc The TeX files are derived from the Font Awesome 5 package, are
longdesc maintained by Daniel Nagel and are released under the LaTeX
longdesc Project Public License version 1.3c. All included fonts are
longdesc provided by Fort Awesome under the SIL OFL 1.1 license. This
longdesc package is not an official Fort Awesome project. For bug
longdesc reports, please open an issue at
longdesc https://github.com/braniii/fontawesome.
